  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Replacement of lost livelihoods assets for most affected households following 2011 floods - DAM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Exceptionally heavy monsoon rain from late July to August 2012 affected or damaged crops, fish/shrimp/crab ponds, other household assets and income generation activities. Approximately 4,277 households of the &#x2018;Improved Food and Livelihood Security&#x2019; (IFLS) programme beneficiaries in Bagerhat district, Bangladesh were affected. 

This grant will support DAM&apos;s response to the needs of beneficiaries who are most affected by the floods: households that lost their livelihoods assets and households that are severely vulnerable owing to the floods. Activities will include strengthening plinths, repairing houses and provision of energy efficient portable stoves.</narrative>
  </description>
